# Git & PR Workflow — RadDash

This file is shared with the team. Every contributor follows these rules. AI agents working in this repo must also follow them.

## Branch Naming

| Who | Pattern | Example |
|-----|---------|---------|
| Phil (backend / full-stack) | `feat/short-description` or `fix/short-description` | `feat/task-detail-page` |
| Hannah (design / UI) | `hannah/feature-name` | `hannah/task-board` |
| RAD devs | `feat/short-description`, `fix/short-description`, `chore/short-description` | `fix/sync-conflict` |

Keep branches focused on one feature or fix. Do not bundle unrelated changes.

## The Golden Rule

**All PRs target `dev`. Never push directly to `main`.** Production releases go through `dev` → `main` via a `release/to-prod` branch.

## Branch Conflict Check — Required Before Starting Any Branch

Before creating a new branch, every agent must:

1. Read `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` — scan the "Files owned" column for overlap with files you plan to touch
2. Cross-reference open PRs: `gh pr list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/rad-dash --state open --json headRefName,title`
3. If any active branch owns files you plan to touch, surface the conflict before proceeding

## Branch Hygiene — Required Before Every Branch Operation

Run `git status --short` before:
- Creating a new branch (`git checkout -b`)
- Switching branches (`git checkout`)
- Running `git add`

If the working tree is not clean, stash before proceeding.

## Before Every PR — Required Steps

```bash
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/dev
git push --force-with-lease

npm run build   # must pass — no TypeScript errors
npm run lint    # must pass — 0 errors
npm run test:unit  # must pass
```

## PR Checklist

- [ ] Branch is rebased on `dev`
- [ ] `npm run build` passes
- [ ] `npm run lint` passes (0 errors)
- [ ] `npm run test:unit` passes
- [ ] New code has a matching test file
- [ ] No secrets committed
- [ ] PR targets `dev` (not `main`)
- [ ] `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` updated while branch is active
- [ ] Delete this branch's row from `ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` when PR merges

## PR Labels

| Label | When to use |
|-------|------------|
| `design` | Hannah's UI/UX work |
| `backend` | API routes, database, auth, server-side logic |
| `dependencies` | Dependency bumps |
| `security` | Security fixes or hardening |
| `chore` | Maintenance, docs, config — no feature change |
| `task-integration` | Work relating to Command Center → RadDash task integration |

## Merge Authority

**Agents must NOT create a PR until the user explicitly approves it.**

After pushing a branch and passing the quality gate:
1. Update `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` — set status to `pushed, awaiting local verify`
2. Tell the user and ask: **"Ready for me to open the PR?"**

Phil's explicit trigger phrases (treat as "yes, create the PR"):
- "create a PR", "open the PR", "go ahead with the PR", "ready for PR", "looks good, PR it", "ship it", "looks good"

## Safe-to-Auto-Merge Conditions (all must be true)

| Condition | How to verify |
|-----------|--------------|
| User approved PR creation | Said yes in chat |
| CI green | All checks `SUCCESS` or `NEUTRAL` |
| Zero unresolved Copilot threads | Thread check query returns no output |
| No merge conflicts | `mergeable: MERGEABLE` |
| PR does NOT touch security-sensitive files | See list below |

### Security-Sensitive Files — Require Phil's Review

- `lib/auth.ts`, `lib/permissions.ts`
- `prisma/schema.prisma`
- Any file containing `PERMISSIONS`, `hasPermission`, or `auth()`
- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`
- Any file handling secrets or environment variables

## Copilot Review

Copilot auto-review is configured via a GitHub Repository Ruleset. It reviews all PRs targeting `dev` and `main`. Address all Copilot comments before merging:

- **Critical/security bugs** → fix in code
- **Style/minor** → log reasoning to skip, resolve the thread
- **Never skip** security or data integrity issues

## Production Deployment

1. Wait for Phil's explicit approval after dev verification
2. Create `release/to-prod` from `origin/dev`
3. Bump version: `npm version patch --no-git-tag-version`
4. Open PR targeting `main` — use `--merge` (never `--squash`)
5. After merge, verify health endpoint, print deploy receipt

## Session Start Protocol — Phil's Agent Only

```bash
# Check pending issues
gh issue list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/rad-dash \
  --label "agent-action-required,deploy-failure,conflict" --state open \
  --json number,title --jq '.[] | "#\(.number): \(.title)"'

# Check open PRs
gh pr list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/rad-dash --state open \
  --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName,isDraft,mergeable \
  --jq '.[] | "#\(.number) [\(.baseRefName)←\(.headRefName)] \(.title) | mergeable:\(.mergeable)"'

# Check prod deploy
gh run list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/rad-dash \
  --workflow deploy.yml --branch main --limit 1 \
  --json databaseId,status,conclusion,headSha \
  --jq 'if length == 0 then "prod: no runs" else .[0] | "prod: \(.status)/\(.conclusion) sha:\(.headSha[0:7])" end'

# Check dev deploy
gh run list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/rad-dash \
  --workflow deploy.yml --branch dev --limit 1 \
  --json databaseId,status,conclusion,headSha \
  --jq 'if length == 0 then "dev: no runs" else .[0] | "dev: \(.status)/\(.conclusion) sha:\(.headSha[0:7])" end'

# Check for approval-needed runs
gh run list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/rad-dash --limit 20 \
  --json databaseId,name,conclusion,headBranch,event \
  --jq '.[] | select(.conclusion == "action_required") | "⚠️ APPROVAL NEEDED: run #\(.databaseId) — \(.name) (branch: \(.headBranch))"'
```

Read `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` and `docs/PENDING_REMINDERS.md` after the above.

## Contributor Agents (RAD dev agents, Hannah's agent)

**Skip the session-start PR queue checks.** Instead:
1. Read `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` to check file ownership conflicts
2. Load relevant `docs/agent-context/` files
3. Register your branch in `ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` before starting work
4. Follow the PR checklist above
5. Do NOT merge PRs or run Railway CLI commands — those belong to Phil
